Notes on judgment calls:

- **Unit 1, 2**: The trailing text after the rejoin ("That's been one" / "Any other value is an") is itself a fresh sentence opening (capitalized, preceded by a period). Leaving it merged onto the rejoined line just relocates the fused violation, so a third line is required — that's why c01-style "rejoin but stop" candidates were rejected in favor of the fuller split (c03/c09).
- **Unit 6**: none of the seven candidates both (a) split the `ends?`/`What` fusion and (b) rejoin `there`/`is` *and* (c) split off the newly-fused `"GC end"?`/`It suffices` boundary — every candidate leaves at least one of the three unresolved, so the correct repair isn't on the list.
- Candidates that split at commas not preceded by a subordinator/coordinating conjunction meeting the "both sides stand alone" test (e.g., breaking right before "and disabled otherwise", or before "the vast majority of which") were rejected as severing a clause rather than following a real boundary.
